course: dictionary
lesson: 15143
title: Smells you can describe
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Scented is an adjective, a describing word. It tells you that something has a nice smell. Look for the clues around it: «The garden was full of scented roses in June.» Roses are sweet-smelling flowers, so scented must mean smelling nice.
explain: Something can be scented in two ways. It can be scented naturally, like a flower, or scented because perfume has been added, like soap. «Mum bought some lightly scented soap» means the soap has a faint, gentle smell.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. Try «smelling nice» in place of scented: «The garden was full of smelling-nice roses in June.» It is a little clumsy, but it still makes sense, so you know you have it right.
fact: Scented means having a nice smell.
fact: Something can be scented naturally, like a rose, or because perfume has been added, like a candle.
fact: Scented is an adjective: it describes a noun, such as «scented candles» or «scented soap».
fact: Many scented flowers, such as lavender, attract bees and butterflies.
fact: Useful phrases: «sweet-scented», «scented candle», «lightly scented».
exercise: «The scented roses filled the garden with sweet smells.» What does scented mean? | Very loud | *Having a nice smell | Covered in sharp thorns | Bright red in colour
exercise: Aunt Amara bought «lightly scented» soap. What does lightly scented mean? | Smelling of smoke | Having no smell at all | Feeling smooth and slippery | *Having a faint, gentle nice smell
exercise: Find the adjective in this sentence: «The bees buzzed around the sweet-scented lavender.» | around | buzzed | bees | *sweet-scented
test: «The scented candle made the whole room smell of apples.» What does scented describe? | The apples | The smoke | The room | *The candle
test: Which word could replace scented in «a scented pen»? | Smelling of rotten eggs | *Smelling sweet | Tasty to eat | Hidden under the desk
exam: «The new soap was scented with lemon, so it smelled fresh in the bath.» What does scented mean here? | Broken into small pieces | Soft to touch | Wet from rain | *Having a nice smell, added on purpose
